==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|владѣ́ть||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|cu|владѣти}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*volděti||to rule}}. 

Compare the inherited doublet {{doublet|ru|володе́ть|notext=1}}. Cognate with {{cog|bg|владе́я||to control, possess}}, {{cog|la|valeō||to be worth, be strong}}, {{cog|en|wield}}, {{cog|de|walten||to rule, prevail}}, {{cog|mk|владее||to govern, be familiar with}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|владе́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-владеть.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-владеть.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|владе́ть|impf|pf=завладе́ть}}

# to [[own]], to [[possess]], to be [[master]] of, to be in [[possession]] of {{+obj|ru|ins<something>}}
# to [[govern]], to [[control]] {{+obj|ru|ins<someone/something>}}
# to [[master]], to [[manage]], to [[wield]] {{+obj|ru|ins<something>}}
#: {{uxi|ru|свобо́дно '''владе́ть''' тру́дным языко́м|'''to wield''' a difficult language easily}}

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|impf-intr|1a|владе́ть}}

